shell.json is GENERATED: edit shell.json.template, not shell.json.

install.sh renders shell.json.template -> shell.json with the private values from the repo's
.env (e.g. ${WEATHER_LOCATION}); shell.json itself is gitignored. Anything written straight into
shell.json (by hand or by Caelestia's settings app) is overwritten on the next render, so copy
such changes into the template. (JSON has no comments, hence this separate note.)

Re-render: cd ~/Dev/Personal/dotfiles && ./install.sh caelestia
Most changes apply live; if one doesn't, restart the shell (Ctrl+Super+Alt+R).
